{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fnmmsaan5gmkl6c5ofktlfa7ltf5j5y2vr4yxu6vgpb6yowqrw4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass.\n\n## Result\n\nThe library is a single function (`void normalize(float*, const float*, int)`), and the Rust translation is **behaviorally identical to the C**. One real defect was found and fixed.\n\n### Bug found & fixed\n**`translation/Cargo.toml`** — with default `debug-assertions`, Rust's `ub_checks` instrumentation converted the unvalidated-input UB paths (null `dest`/`src`, negative `size`) into a controlled `abort()`, so the debug-profile `.so` died with **SIGABRT(6)** where the C dies with **SIGSEGV(11)**. Disabled `debug-assertions`/`overflow-checks` for `dev`/`test` so every profile reproduces C's observable behavior. (`overflow-checks` mattered too: C's `i += 1` wraps silently.)\n\n`src/lib.rs` needed no changes — the sequential `f32` accumulator, `1.0f/sqrtf` reciprocal, `> 0.0f` NaN-unordered branch, `dest != src` pointer guard, and the sign-extending/wrapping `size * sizeof(float)` memset length were all already exact.\n\n### Phase artifacts (`translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C exports exactly 1 symbol (`normalize`); symbol diff **empty**; all Rust imports are libc/unwind. No C module was left untranslated, no stubs.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 15 rows. The C validates *nothing* (no `return -1`, no asserts, no null/range checks), so the surface is branch selection + UB. All 15 rows have passing differential tests, including 7 **fault-parity** rows that fork one child per side and assert the identical `wait(2)` status (verified as real `SIGSEGV(11)`, not \"both failed somehow\").\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 20 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: both `if` branches × pointer aliasing (separate / `dest==src` / forward & backward overlap) × 23 sizes × 12 value classes (normals, wide exponents, powers of two, `FLT_MAX` overflow, subnormals, `±0.0`, NaN payloads, `±inf`, random bit patterns) × misalignment. All 20 pass.\n\n### Testing approach\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and compared over the **entire backing allocation as raw `u32` words** (so `-0.0` vs `+0.0`, NaN payloads, and out-of-window writes are all caught), with poison guards around every window.\n\n**Sensitivity proven** via `mutation_check.sh`: 16 injected mutations, 14 caught. The 2 uncaught are **provably equivalent mutants**, not gaps — `sum.abs() > 0.0` is identical because `sum` can never be negative or `-0.0`; `saturating_mul` vs `wrapping_mul` differ only for negative sizes, where both lengths are ~18 exabytes and fault on the same page.\n\n**Matrix (`verify_all.sh`): 18/18 cells green** — 3 feature configs (`default`, `--no-default-features`, `--all-features`; no `[features]` declared) × Rust release+debug × C at `-O0`/`-O2`/`-O3`, 45 tests each.\n\nNotes: no `add_executable` in `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`, so the stdout-comparison gate is N/A (asserted by a test). `c_src/` was not modified. Crates were fetched with `--offline` from the local cargo cache since the sandbox proxy blocks crates.io."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_read_input_tokens":105671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1022,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"498e1878-ba96-458a-aa48-bcd7b079ed66","uuid":"25c50fdd-19ae-402a-8462-64e26415b060","timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:35:21.364Z"}
